From f739a726a613eb6135c4c5e57fe54c7a48794ece Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 05:56:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] perf(gateway): coalesce concurrent resolver lookups and
 cache misses briefly

When a cached entry expired, every request that arrived before the
first lookup finished queried the control plane on its own, and a
missing or not-yet-ready service was queried again by every request.

Concurrent misses for the same tenant, namespace and service now share
one lookup. The lookup does not follow the cancellation of the request
that started it, so the other waiters and the cache still get the
result. "Not found", "not Ready" and "no usable endpoints" are cached
for one second (never longer than the resolver TTL); 403, other
control-plane errors and network errors are still not cached.
